sources.place_summary:
Cobb Mountain Art & Ecology Project in Middletown, CA, offers wood-fire and soda firing opportunities. Potters can participate through dated workshops (wood anagama, train kiln, and soda firings), ongoing membership after attending 2+ workshops for 2 seasons, or residencies (short-term 1-2 months, long-term 10-12 months, or specialized wood-fire 1-year positions) that include access to a 250 cu. ft. anagama, 60 cu. ft. train kiln, and a 25 cu. ft. cross-draft wood/gas/soda/salt kiln.",
    "notes": "The tea bowl workshop (September 12 & 13) was excluded because the page does not mention firing or that the pieces will be fired in a kiln. Most 2026-2027 workshops are sold out or on waitlist. Instagram posts mention a September soda firing workshop led by Casey Beck that occurred before today (2026-09-25 post references 'last weekend' firing); an August salt firing workshop; and a 'Manzanita Madness 2' wood firing, but none of these provide specific dates within the 12-month window or registration information. The 'Plates Plates Plates' workshop (August 15) on Instagram is a mold-making and plate-building workshop with no mention of firing in the kiln and was excluded. Only opportunities with firing in kilns or pits were recorded."
  }
